<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Cook asked for a same-day visit. Two nights ago he woke with severe pain in his right big toe; by morning the joint was red, hot and swollen, and he could not bear the bedsheet on it. He has not injured it. He has never had this before. He has no fever or chills and no other painful joints. He has walked only a little since, in a slipper. He took acetaminophen, which barely helped. He started hydrochlorothiazide seven weeks ago, with amlodipine, atorvastatin and aspirin, and has taken all of them. He has had no muscle aches. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Two nights ago, waking him from sleep</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Right big toe joint</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About 36 hours</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Throbbing; cannot bear the bedsheet</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>8 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Constant, worst the first morning</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Hydrochlorothiazide for seven weeks; no injury; no previous attacks</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Acetaminophen barely helps; worse with any pressure</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Redness and swelling; no fever or chills; no other joints</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

